course: everyday
lesson: 463
title: The best friend who moves away
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Maddie's family is moving to Australia. Lily finds out a month before, and they cry in the school toilets until the bell. On her last day Maddie gives everyone a cupcake. Kieran, who teased her for years, mumbles, «Gonna miss you, Mads, no cap,» — «no cap» means «for real, no lie» — and goes red when she hugs him. They make a plan: a video call every Saturday. Because of the time difference, it's Saturday morning for Lily and Saturday evening in Perth, the big city of Western Australia.
explain: First call from Perth: Maddie shows her new uniform with a big hat and says, «It's heaps hot, I'm wearing thongs.» Lily is horrified — until Maddie explains that in Australia thongs are flip-flops and «heaps» means loads. They laugh till they cry, and Lily starts a list of Aussie words. But by month three Maddie misses two Saturdays because of netball, and Lily feels forgotten. Instead of sulking, they pick a new time that works for both. The calls get shorter, but steadier.
explain: Lily keeps saying no to Priya, a new girl who wants to be friends, because «Maddie's my best friend». On a call, Maddie says, «Make new friends, you dafty, I have!» Lily lets Priya in. A new friend doesn't betray an old one. Connor's mate Liam moves to Canada; his first message: «got a toque and a double-double, i'm basically Canadian now, eh». Connor looks both up: a toque is a woolly hat, a double-double is coffee with two creams and two sugars. They game together online on Fridays, with their parents' OK.
explain: Not every friendship survives a move. Jake's best friend Ryan moves across town and changes school. «We'll still hang out,» Ryan says. They meet twice, then stop. A year later they bump into each other in town and chat happily for ten minutes. Nobody did anything wrong; it's just harder without seeing each other every day. Sam's friend Ade goes to Nigeria for a year and they write real letters. Ade's reply takes two months and has a stamp with a bird on it. Mia, who moved from Georgia to Ohio, now gets told she says «y'all» funny in both places.
fact: Moving away is one of the hardest things for a friendship, and it is normal to feel very sad.
fact: Making a plan together, like a regular call, helps a long-distance friendship.
fact: Time zones mean it can be a different time of day in another country; Australia is many hours ahead of Britain.
fact: Friends who move will build new lives, so being flexible about calls works better than sulking.
fact: Making a new friend does not betray an old one; you can have both.
fact: Some friendships fade after a move even when nobody did anything wrong, and you can still be glad of them.
fact: Letters and parcels are slow, but they can keep a friendship going for years.
fact: Playing online with faraway friends should be done with your parents' agreement.
fact: Goodbyes often show how people really feel, even people who teased you.
fact: Moving can make you feel between two places, and both sets of friends are yours.
fact: In Australia «thongs» are flip-flops and «heaps» means lots; in Canada a «toque» is a woolly hat and a «double-double» is coffee with two creams and two sugars.
fact: «No cap» is young people's slang for «for real, no lie».
exercise: What plan did Lily and Maddie make before the move? | A video call every Saturday | A long letter every five years | Never to make any new friends | To swap houses for a year
exercise: Why is it Saturday evening for Maddie when it's Saturday morning for Lily? | Australia is many hours ahead in time | Maddie stays up very late every night | Australia has much longer days in winter | Lily's clock is broken
exercise: «I'm wearing thongs.» What are thongs in Australia? | Flip-flops | Welly boots | School socks | Swimming caps
exercise: Maddie missed two calls because of netball. What did they do? | Picked a new time that worked for both | Stopped being friends | Lily joined the netball team by video every week | Shouted at each other
exercise: Why did Maddie start missing calls? | She was busy with her new life | She didn't like Lily any more | Her phone was banned | She forgot Lily's name
exercise: Why did Lily keep saying no to Priya? | She thought it would betray Maddie | Priya had been rude to her on the first day | Priya didn't speak English | Her mum told her to
exercise: What did Maddie say about new friends? | «Make new friends, I have!» | «Never replace me, promise me» | «Only make friends with boys» | «Wait till I come back home»
exercise: Does having a new friend betray an old one? | No, you can have both | Yes, every single time | Only if they're in the same class | Only if you tell them about it
exercise: What happened to Jake and Ryan after Ryan changed school? | They met twice, then stopped | They became closer than ever | They had a huge fight | Ryan moved back next door
exercise: When Jake and Ryan met in town a year later, how was it? | Friendly, they chatted for ten minutes | They walked past and ignored each other | They had a fight | They cried together for an hour
exercise: How did Sam and Ade keep in touch? | They wrote real letters | They sent carrier pigeons | They never kept in touch | They called every single hour
exercise: «Got a toque.» What is a toque in Canada? | A woolly hat | A hockey stick | A canoe for the lake | A maple syrup jar
exercise: What is a double-double? | Coffee with two creams and two sugars | A double cheeseburger with two slices of cheese | A two-storey bus | A hockey score
exercise: Kieran said «gonna miss you, Mads, no cap». What does «no cap» mean? | For real, no lie | Without a hat | No more teasing you | Goodbye forever
exercise: What does Kieran's goodbye show? | Goodbyes show how people really feel | He was glad she was going | He was only joking | He wanted a second cupcake
exercise: Mia now feels «in-between» Georgia and Ohio. What's true? | Both sets of friends are hers | She has to pick one place to belong to | She has no friends in either | She must change her accent
test: «she's not answered for 2 weeks, she's forgot me, I'm done with her». What's wiser? | Talk and find a new time, she's just busy | Block her straight away so she knows how it feels | Send her angry messages | Tell everyone she's fake
test: Lily: «if I make friends with Priya it's like cheating on Maddie». Is she right? | No, a new friend doesn't betray an old one | Yes, you can only have one real best friend at a time | Yes, unless Maddie agrees in writing | No, but she must hide it
test: If Lily rings at 8am on Saturday in England, what is it like in Perth? | Already Saturday afternoon or evening | Still Friday night | Exactly 8am | Sunday morning
test: Jake: «Ryan said we'd hang out and we didn't, he's a liar». What's fairer? | It's just harder without seeing each other daily | Ryan was always planning to dump him once he'd moved | Jake did something wrong | Friends who move always lie
test: «letters are dead old-school, nobody does that». What did Sam and Ade find? | Letters were slow but special | Letters never arrive | Letters only work in Nigeria | Letters cost too much to send
test: Your mate's moving to Canada and says «we'll game every Friday». What should you check first? | That your parents are OK with it | That the game is the newest | That your mate pays for it | Nothing at all
test: Kieran teased Maddie for years, then says he'll miss her. What's going on? | Goodbyes often show how people really feel | He's planning one last big prank before she goes | He wants her cupcake | He's being sarcastic
test: In a film, best friends who move apart stay exactly the same forever with no effort. What's real? | Friends far away need effort and flexibility | Distance never changes anything | Friends always forget each other | You need a spaceship to stay friends
test: Maddie says she's «wearing thongs to school». Lily gasps. What should Lily do? | Ask what the word means there | Report Maddie to the teacher | Hang up in shock | Pretend she understood
test: Imagine Lily refused all new friends until Maddie came back. What would most likely happen? | Lily would be lonely for years | Maddie would come back sooner | Lily would be happier | Priya would move to Perth
test: «mia talks proper weird now, saying y'all». What's happened? | She picked up words from where she lived | She's just showing off to look cool | She's forgotten English | She's in a play
exam: Identify the measure most likely to sustain a friendship following the relocation of one friend to another continent. | An agreed and regular arrangement for communication | The abandonment of all new friendships | An undertaking never to change one's activities | Communication exclusively by surface mail once a decade
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the formation of a new friendship whilst a former close friend resides abroad? | It does not constitute a betrayal of the former friend | It necessarily terminates the former friendship | It requires the written consent of the former friend | It is prohibited until the former friend returns
exam: Given that it is eight o'clock on Saturday morning in the United Kingdom, ascertain the time of day in Western Australia. | Afternoon or evening of the same Saturday | Night of the preceding Friday | Precisely eight o'clock on Saturday morning | Morning of the following Sunday
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning friendships that diminish after one party changes school. | They may fade without fault on either side | They fade solely because one party has lied | They fade only when a quarrel has first occurred | They cannot fade if both parties are sincere
